  "question": "What does Part 5.2 require, and which of our own documents shows that we actually do it?",
  "answer": "I need to be upfront: the standard text does not contain a \"Part 5.2\" in the CIP-007-6 R2 framework. The four Parts of CIP-007-6 R2 are 2.1, 2.2, 2.3, and 2.4. The only \"5.2\" I found in the operator's documents is in the CIP-008 Incident Response Plan (section 5.2 \"Protect\"), which is a different CIP standard.\n\nLet me confirm what the operator's own documents actually say about the patch management process, since that's the most likely candidate for what you're asking about.\n\nCited sections:\n- isection-54b1a51296c6c865638a (Technical Feasible Exceptions, CIP-005/LSPG TFE Procedure v4.pdf) \u2014 shows Part 5.1, 5.6, and 5.7 of CIP-007-6 R2 are referenced in the TFE procedure, but does not contain Part 5.2\n- isection-440a5cdf9a6b65292ef3 (intentional_strictness on CIP-007-6 R2 Part 2.2) \u2014 operator note about 30-day evaluation cadence vs. the 35-day standard\n- isection-87d00aedd4cf1f41f0cd (CIP-002-5.1a, \u00a73.4.2.1) \u2014 operator's patch management process policy text\n- isection-5a6e77a9acc7ab5eee74 (CIP-002-5.1a, \u00a73.1.2) \u2014 procedure text on tracking sources\n- isection-21a30e0d44708f5dfdce (CIP-002-5.1a, \u00a73.3.1\u20133.3.2) \u2014 procedure text on evaluation cadence\n\nWhat I have not read: the actual text of CIP-007-6 R2 Part 5.2. The standard's four Parts are 2.1, 2.2, 2.3, and 2.4 \u2014 there is no Part 5.2 in CIP-007-6 R2. The \"5.2\" in the operator's documents is from CIP-008 (Incident Response Plan), which is a different standard.\n\nIf you are looking for a specific Part 5.2 requirement, it may be in a different CIP standard (e.g., CIP-005-7, CIP-010-4, or another standard) that I have not located. Could you clarify which CIP standard or which Part 5.2 you are referring to?",
